{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792169987,"nonce":"siFNMlbiuJGVg1spw3GCTcVY3DI=","title":"WindowedApp has no way to veto a window close request","message":"ashui/app/WindowedApp.hx quits as soon as it sees\nwindow.Event.Closed/Destroyed (`case Closed | Destroyed: quitting = true`),\nwith no way for the app to intervene. Reported need, from ChimpMonk's\neditor: asking Save / Discard / Cancel on quit when there are unsaved\nedits.\n\nhlwindow's Closed event already supports this per its own doc (\"It\nstays open until `close`\"), so the window layer doesn't need to\nchange. Suggested shape: a WindowConfig.onCloseRequest:Void-\u003eBool\ncallback (false keeps the window open; the app calls\nWindowedApp.quit() itself later once its own confirmation flow\nresolves).","files":null}]}